## Imagery
- Sentinel-2 cloudless 2016 - https://s2maps.eu by EOX IT Services GmbH (Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data
  2016 & 2017), CC BY 4.0. Layer s2cloudless_3857. Only the 2016 release is used (later releases are CC BY-NC-SA).
  - Globe: zoom 4, assets/world.jpg copied from ../dp_maps (URLs in raw/manifest_world.jsonl); a bright cloud streak over
    Ireland is replaced by the local median colour (tools/fix_world.py) — "modified".
  - Sealand: wide patch zoom 9 (1.2 W–3.4 E, 50.9–53.4 N), medium zoom 11 (0.7–2.1 E, 51.55–52.3 N),
    detailed zoom 13 (1.22–1.62 E, 51.83–52.03 N).
  - Liberland: wide zoom 9 (16.6–21.2 E, 44.4–47.0 N), medium zoom 11 (18.45–19.35 E, 45.45–46.05 N),
    detailed zoom 13 (18.76–18.99 E, 45.69–45.84 N).
  - Hutt River: wide zoom 9 (111.8–117.6 E, 31.0–25.6 S), medium zoom 11 (113.85–115.05 E, 28.55–27.6 S),
    detailed zoom 13 (114.33–114.62 E, 28.17–27.98 S). The rest of Australia is the globe texture.
  - Modified: colour-graded like the globe (land warmed, a little less saturation); the outer quarter of each wide patch fades
    into the globe texture, the outer tenth of each medium / detailed patch into the patch around it. Sealand and Hutt River
    (SEA=.75 in tools/fetch_patch.py): the open sea (big connected areas at or below 0 m in the AWS terrain) is pulled toward
    the flat sea colour of the globe, and farther than ~4 km from land it is smoothed (σ 8 km), so the hard edge between the
    turbid near-shore water and the flat fill of the mosaic in the North Sea becomes a soft gradient. Land is untouched.
- Elevation: AWS Terrain Tiles (Mapzen / Tilezen "terrarium" PNG), zoom 9, 11 and 13, https://registry.opendata.aws/terrain-tiles/
  (sources include SRTM, GMTED, ETOPO1, GEBCO). True scale, no exaggeration (all three places are low and flat).
- Liberland outline: OpenStreetMap relation 19735507 «Siga» (boundary=disputed), fetched via the Nominatim API
  (nominatim.openstreetmap.org/lookup?osm_ids=R19735507&polygon_geojson=1), assets/siga_osm.json. © OpenStreetMap contributors,
  ODbL 1.0 (https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright). Area of the ring on the sphere: 7.08 km² → «≈ 7 км²» as the narration says.
